(skill-contract
  (name "pr-flow")
  (v "ημ.skill/pr-flow@0.3.2")

  (intent
    "Route every pull-request interaction through the pr-flow state machine (flow.edn): muse, plan, planning review, ready, red, green, code review, merge gate, merged, reflected. Ships an nbb CLI over pure .cljc laws for GitHub review mechanics.")

  (activation
    (priority 80)
    (explicit ["skill:pr-flow"])
    (triggers ["pull request" "PR" "draft PR" "coderabbit" "@coderabbitai" "review comment" "review thread"
               "resolve thread" "auto-merge" "merge the PR" "sprint planning" "epic and stories"]))

  (governance
    (touch-layer :mutable)
    (non-override [:mission :directives :safety :license :output-shape])
    (requires-user-approval false))

  (effects
    (writes true)
    (network true)
    (commits true))

  (invariants
    (positive-bot-thread-cohort "Version2 declares one sorted unique exact native thread/root vector under one repository/PR/current head and one immutable complete corpus/source carrier. One actual authorized User proposal and one distinct configured assessor publication explicitly cover EVERY member with a judgment/reason/evidence bijection; missing/extra/duplicate/reordered/finding/uncertain/mixed rows refuse all. The only issue extension is that exact proposal plus assessment. Every declared terminal writer candidate must independently pass native User/permission/root/head/source/chronology/writer-review validation before normalized base custody can qualify; resolved without writer emits no qualified observation. Whole-cohort phase history permits only pending to verified actual append to resolved advancement, never source/head/target edits, unknown participants, deletion/reopening/restoration. One-target guarded native effects preserve simultaneous known member proofs without broad interleaving or credit. Model transport/full-input/runtime qualification remains separately required; existing informational/rejection hosts do not by themselves supply a cohort publication adapter.")
    (positive-bot-thread-preservation "Separate exact repository name/database/node profile and native root-publisher tuple, without new approval/assessor/rejection/withdrawal authority for that publisher. Preserve root/prose/P1/native history as findings. Complete Bot ID custody, all ordered native conversation/review/issue context, immutable relevant source text/Git-blob/SHA256 and complete purpose-specific admission/revocation history bind an actual authorized unedited User proposal to an actual distinct configured assessor's substantive preservation judgment. Retain preservation requests; mixed defects/corrective requests/unresolved questions, finding/uncertain judgment, incomplete/stale/changed source and copied informational/rejection records fail closed. Same physical App cannot corroborate itself through another model label; accepted independent full-input inference/runtime evidence remains an outer obligation. No semantic regex or root-ID exemption.")
    (positive-bot-thread-transition "Specialized Handled prefix guards before generic writes, using one fixed GitHub.com token-stripped/keyring environment and actual full User/permission refresh. Exactly one reply attempt followed by complete actual matching native reply/readback; no hypothetical writer or invented ID/time. Verify unchanged prior corpus and exactly one actual writer append/count increment, then refresh full history/actor and attempt one resolution. Final readback admits only that append and resolution flag change. Unknown/partial outcomes stay uncertain without credential fallback/retry. Classification/assessment or reply without actual resolution remains blocking. Blocker law recomputes actual proof; later changes/disputes/withdrawal revoke source IDs permanently through the canonical append-only purpose-isolated history. Prospective APIs supply only exact text/bindings/future creation conditions. No approval/coverage/cohort/round/CI/deployment/installation or protected source bootstrap credit.")
    (prospective-assessment-publication "Pure assessment-publication shares actual disposition evaluation and strict protocol/payload predicates. Fresh canonical classification with a positive-ID withdrawal set, complete history, native context, latest authorized unedited proposal and repository-scoped prospective Bot eligibility are required. Return only an exact two-line body, existing context/proposal bindings, expected principal and future creation-after requirement; no synthetic assessment ID/time/URL/hash/observation/qualified disposition. A configured tuple is not live App authentication or accepted independent invocation. Real POST/readback must subsequently qualify unchanged disposition; unresolved conversations and all other gates remain unchanged. Source preparation is unadopted and supplies no native publication or review credit.")
    (complete-actionability-history "Importable observations decoder preserves actual edamame one-map-per-nonblank-line validation and repository binding before selection. Complete decoded UTF-8 source text is caller supplied; nil/invalid source returns unavailable nil and valid empty returns []. CLI retains actual module-relative read/error and append effects. Code pinning does not prove fresh revocation history; outer source bytes/digest/acquisition custody is required. No parser/runtime import manufactures current history authority.")
    (proxx-kimi-publication "Separate Proxx-only exact Bot numeric/node/type admission verifies native run/attempt/jobs, GitHub artifact/ZIP/submission hashes, immutable workflow merge parents and reviewed source bytes, runtime/base ancestry, full-input provenance and native review/inline/body readback. No login, self-tag, model summary, generic GHA or success label alone is authority; no candidate source executes or App token exchange occurs. Global Kimi identities remain empty and OpenCode corroboration stays separate; one physical App cannot supply independent self-corroboration or two provider votes.")
    (proxx-kimi-credit "API diagnostics/actionability supply zero coverage/completion/approval. Verified finding-bearing COMMENTED full publications complete without approving; passing explicit verdicts require no inline findings and existing exact-head/incomplete-scope guards; the observed artifact sentence is evaluated as normal prose, rejecting quoted/generated examples and negative reversals. A later full nonpassing publication clears this principal's earlier passing verdict on that head. Preserve historical configured rosters, add Kimi only to the current Proxx cohort, keep mandatory overrides/required checks and authenticated quota rules. Source proposal/fixtures are not installation, enrollment, current native approval or historical credit transfer. Missing/expired/changed native proof fails closed.")
    (state-machine "flow.edn is lawful per pr-flow.flow/problems; every named skill exists.")
    (configuration-boundary "Only consumed flow/defaults configure the CLI. Review settlement and merge-default behavior, intended invitations and the emitted github-approved/explicit-review-verdict/explicit-issue-verdict channel names are documented as non-executable notes; invitation intent is not dispatch or availability evidence.")
    (card-authority "Card status moves only through Rheos; flow states only name the expected transition.")
    (settle-before-resolve "Every finding thread gets a Fixed|Handled|Deferred|Rejected reply before it is resolved. Every thread defaults to a finding; independently admitted informational disposition is not settlement and never clears an unresolved conversation.")
    (settlement-authority "Only repository-writer settlements count; the finding's opener cannot settle their own pushback in either threads or review bodies. Review-body settlement requires known, distinct author identities.")
    (review-body-discovery "Every provider and human is included; body-only requests and legacy listed findings have stable whole-review IDs and a verified Fixed settlement path.")
    (native-positive-body-settlement "Stable unique CodeRabbit body IDs retain conservative fallback severity. Only exact complete authored LGTM file groups in the bounded Additional-comments format, configured native Bot identity, observed native review/source/time and a distinct true-authorized native User writer with live exact-current-head item prose and strictly later creation/edit chronology qualify an existing Handled disposition. Unknown, malformed, nested, quoted, fenced, generated, duplicate or mixed-negative input and genuine P0/P1 findings remain conservative; no per-item allowlist or blanket Handled-P1 admission. Historical source head is retained separately from current writer/head custody. No approval, coverage, rejection, cohort, round, required-check, deployment or adoption credit is created.")
    (snapshot-consistency "Approval evidence precedes conversation reads and is rechecked afterward; gate application refreshes evidence immediately before the guarded merge.")
    (verified-findings "During the first five rounds, fix verified findings regardless of priority, preferably exactly as requested when lawful and verified. Do not defer merely for priority or volume; exceptions need detailed user-authorized reasoning.")
    (independent-rejection "An outright rejection requires detailed reasoning, code or test evidence, and explicit finding/head-bound agreement from another agent besides CodeRabbit. CodeRabbit assent and author self-agreement never qualify.")
    (native-issue-rejection "Authenticated allowlisted non-CodeRabbit Bot PR issue comments may corroborate a thread rejection only with one live exact-current-head agreement marker and exact native thread/root-comment binding shared by the writer proposal. Complete paginated issue context is collected on thread/settle/gate paths. Creation must follow the latest proposal/edit; publication/edit must precede the matching final writer settlement. Missing/ambiguous/generated scope, opener self-corroboration, stale heads and later scoped pushback block. Preserve source channel, native ID and URL; a completed assessment is not approval, full-review or round credit, and later workflow cancellation never waives a required check.")
    (native-source-withdrawal "Authenticated same-Bot explicit withdrawal of a current finding/head-bound agreement by its native issue-comment ID or exact source URL revokes that source, even after settlement, without requiring a repeated Finding pair. A same-Bot thread-only withdrawal blocks that thread's ambiguous agreement. Quoted/forged/unrelated references never revoke other evidence; withdrawing an older source does not revoke a subsequent independently qualified source. Preserve complete native context and compare raw source snapshots independently of approval-specific commit hydration.")
    (native-opener-withdrawal "A configured authenticated Bot may explicitly withdraw its own current-head inline finding with specific live rationale and source links. This is finding supersession, not author rejection or independent corroboration. Preserve original severity/root/review/withdrawal IDs and history. Complete ordered native context, matching opener identity, repository/PR/thread/root/head, current native enclosing reviews, no later conflict/edit and resolved native conversation are required. Only an authorized User's Handled reply naming that head, exact Finding pair and native withdrawal URL completes settlement; reviewer auto-resolution alone does not. Quotes/generated examples, missing/ambiguous evidence, author/different-opener claims, stale heads, cross-root scope and later pushback remain blockers. No approval, coverage, round, quorum or check credit is supplied.")
    (informational-candidate "Separately consumed provisional review/actionability policy retains verified native OpenCode identity and adds the observed native MiMo tuple only for exact open-hax/proxx with native repository ID 1178288746 and open-hax/knoxx with native repository ID 1199983316, not the rejection or approval identity lists. Protocol withdrawals remain exact same-Bot source withdrawals. Initial scope requires resolved author-only User threads and empty native enclosing COMMENTED reviews. A distinct resolved-author-only-commented-review-context scope binds nonempty author COMMENTED bodies for whole-context independent assessment; missing body metadata has no scope. The distinct unresolved-author-only-commented-review-context scope requires matching false resolution flags and nonempty author COMMENTED bodies, preserving complete independent admission. Qualified unresolved informational conversations remain unsettled and all-thread merge-blocking. Every actual finding retains settle-before-resolve and opener exclusion. Exact repository/PR/current-head/thread/root, complete ordered context, body/hunk hashes, native IDs and edit metadata bind a fresh writer proposal to independent native issue assessment with substantive reason/evidence. Native identity is observed publication evidence, not runtime/model/App-key independence or overall-run-success proof. Parent authorized isolated preparation; source/profile review and actual fresh native assessment remain prerequisites to operational use.")
    (informational-resolution-eligibility "Pure resolution-authorization consumes canonically classified native context with the existing derived positive-ID withdrawal set and recomputes complete disposition. Raw/malformed input or caller classification flags cannot supply eligibility. A positive binding is not native provenance, actor permission, a GitHub effect or settlement/approval/round/check credit. The pure function adds no collector/resolver/transport. The separate candidate resolve-informational CLI must be protected, reviewed and adopted before use. It freshly collects and classifies rather than accepting supplied sets, compares exact expected native coordinates, authenticates a native User writer separately from the configured Bot assessor in one fixed gh environment, refreshes complete native/history/identity/permission input, attempts one resolution POST without a reply or retry, and retains actual response/readback/revocation custody. Uncertain outcomes remain uncertain. Resolution changes the real manifest and requires new resolved-scope proposal/assessment. Actual original unresolved conversations stay blocked; reviewed source/adoption and real native assessment remain required.")
    (informational-isolation "One canonical finding-obligation predicate governs severity/settlement/contestation/deferral/convergence. Informational remains unsettled and supplies zero approval, coverage, rejection or round credit. Unresolved conversations, other findings/review bodies, all deterministic checks, quorum/cohort/minimum and branch protection remain unchanged. Mechanical binding/length/syntax cannot guarantee semantic correctness or independent reasoning; native semantic assessment still requires review.")
    (informational-revocation "Changed head/comments/enclosing reviews, edits/restoration, new participants, incomplete context, missing source, conflicts and same-Bot exact-source withdrawals revoke admission. Reuse the existing withdrawal grammar with the separately admitted identity. CLI appends canonical Receipt River admission/revocation observations and rehydrates before guarded merge; observed revoked native IDs cannot be restored. No thread allowlists, candidate flags, semantic classifier regex or native transcript impersonation. Disposition itself has no GitHub effect; only the separately protected/adopted resolve-informational adapter may perform its explicit qualified administration, without settlement or approval credit.")
    (review-convergence "Five completed review rounds is a soft minimum, never a hard cap. Early exit requires unanimous current-head approval by available agents plus settlement of every finding. Continue beyond five while findings or gates remain unresolved.")
    (legacy-stage-provenance "An authorized native User's unedited legacy pr-flow-head declaration with one live exact full head marker and one planning/code stage marker is stage history on that PR. Preserve native ID/head/time and apply the existing timestamp boundary; no retroactive first-stage binding is introduced. Missing/ambiguous/quoted/generated/edited or public non-writer declarations do not qualify. Planning-to-code transitions, current-head approval, eligible complete review cohorts, quota/incomplete/revoked evidence and required checks retain their existing laws. A stage declaration alone supplies no review, approval, completed round or model-identity credit.")
    (available-agent-cohort "All available agents; authenticated quota observations exclude optional agents only; per-review notices bind the current head, while the observed Codex account-quota format also covers automatic App runs and preserves any original request head across pushes, never mandatory reviewers. Preserve native IDs/time/reset, restore on expiry/new request/new completion, and retain historical full-roster counts. A current complete available pass supplies at most one cohort, with no quota approval/review credit.")
